              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# ROLE\nYou are a Data Processing Engine. You must compute a unique union count from 3 JSON objects and return ONE valid JSON object.\n\n# DATASETS\nEach tag contains ONE JSON object of the form:\n{ \"NegotiationsList\": [ { \"AuctionHeaderId\": \"...\", \"Status\": \"...\", \"DifferenceInDays\": <number> }, ... ] }\n\n<Drafts>\n{{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_DRAFT_NEGOTIATIONS.$output.result}}\n</Drafts>\n\n<Approvals>\n{{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_APPROVAL_IN_PROCESS_DATA.$output.result}}\n</Approvals>\n\n<NotApprovedNegs>\n{{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_NOT_APPROVED_DATA.$output.result}}\n</NotApprovedNegs>\n\n# ALGORITHM\n1) Parse the JSON inside each tag and iterate ONLY over its NegotiationsList array.\n2) Draft matches:\n   - Include AuctionHeaderId if Status == \"DRAFT\" AND DifferenceInDays >= 5.000\n3) Approval matches:\n   - Include AuctionHeaderId if Status == \"APPROVAL_IN_PROCESS\" AND DifferenceInDays >= 3.000\n4) NotApproved matches:\n   - Include AuctionHeaderId if Status == \"REJECTED\" OR Status == \"WITHDRAWN\".\n5) Merge all matched IDs into ONE set (dedupe across ALL datasets).\n6) Count = size of the set (integer).\n\n# OUTPUT (STRICT)\nReturn valid JSON only. No markdown. No extra keys.\n\n{\n  \"ReportType\": \"TOTAL_COUNT\",\n  \"Bucket\": \"BEFORE_PUBLISH\",\n  \"Count\": <Integer>\n}"
            }
