              "value": "# ROLE\nYou are a data processing engine. You must compute a unique union count from 2 JSON objects that include a list of negotiation and return ONE valid JSON object with the total count.\n\n# DATASETS\n\n<Active>\n{{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_ACTIVE_DATA.$output.result}}\n</Active>\n\n<Paused>\n{{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_PAUSED_DATA.$output.result}}\n</Paused>\n\n# ALGORITHM\n1) Parse the JSON inside each tag and iterate ONLY over its NegotiationsList array.\n2) Active matches:\n   - Include AuctionHeaderId if Status == \"ACTIVE\" AND  DifferenceInDays <= 5.000\n3) Paused matches:\n   - Include  AuctionHeaderId if Status == \"PAUSED\" .\n4) Count = active matches + paused matches.\n\n# OUTPUT FORMAT\n-Return valid JSON object only. No markdown. No extra keys. \n-MUST NOT include matchedIds as a JSON attribute.\n-You MUST Always Include the \"Bucket\" attribute with the value \"IN_PROGRESS\".\n-Include the count attribute.\n\nJSON output extrict format:\n{\n  \"ReportType\": \"TOTAL_COUNT\",\n  \"Bucket\": \"IN_PROGRESS\",\n  \"Count\": <Count>,\n  \"Paused\": <Get the count from here {{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_PAUSED_DATA.$output.result}}>,\n  \"Active\": <Get the count from here {{$context.$nodes.SIMPLIFY_ACTIVE_DATA.$output.result}}>\n}"
            }
